  "final": "The suite passes again. It had one failing test, `test_parse_european_decimal`, and one changed line fixed it.\n\n**Cause:** `parse_amount` in `pipeline/parse.py:18` cut the decimal part of European-style amounts to one digit (`frac[:1]`). So `\"1.234,56\"` parsed as `1234.5` instead of `1234.56`.\n\n**Changed:** `pipeline/parse.py`: `frac[:1]` is now `frac`.\n\n**Verified:** `python3 -m unittest` exited 1 before the fix (`AssertionError: 1234.5 != 1234.56`, 1 of 151 tests failing). After the fix it exits 0 with \"Ran 151 tests ... OK\".\n\nI didn't add a regression test, because the existing test already covers this case. I also didn't run a bisect. The repo has a single commit, so there was nothing to bisect.",
